[0.006, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Did our signups fall from last month?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 92s over 8 steps, 25,130 tokens, 21 observations gathered, 10 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Cannot be confirmed: the data needed to compare recent signups to last month is missing for most of the relevant window — all signup and session sources stop returning rows after 2026-08-12, so neither the rest of August nor September can be measured.  [posthog.event_trend 031f54a8, ga4.get_sessions d624355c, posthog.event_trend f3a69518]\r\n  In the days that do have data (August 1-12), the daily signup rate was flat at roughly 150-163 per day, showing no sign of decline within that partial window.  [posthog.event_trend 031f54a8]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Dat"]
[0.000, "o", "a coverage ends August 12  (medium)\r\n    - Posthog signup, pageview, and trial event data, and GA4 session data, all stop returning rows after 2026-08-12, so neither August (fully) nor September can be compared to July.  [posthog.event_trend 031f54a8, posthog.event_trend ae570c02, ga4.get_sessions d624355c, posthog.event_trend a79c6f00, posthog.event_trend f3a69518]\r\n    - Within the days that do have data (2026-08-01 through 2026-08-12), the daily signup rate was stable at roughly 150-163 per day, showing no decline within that window.  [posthog.event_trend 031f54a8]\r\n    - A GA4 comparison of 2026-08-01–21 against 2026-07-01–21 shows sessions down 44% and conversions down 44%, but the GA4 series for that same August window has no rows past August 12, so most of the 'current' period is missing data rather than a real decline.  [ga4.compare_periods e58f6ec6, ga4.get_sessions d624355c]\r\n    - A team member raised the same concern in Slack on 2026-08-11, asking whether signups looked down for the month, whi"]
[0.000, "o", "ch is consistent with the same partial-month data being misread as a real drop.  [slack.search_messages 57c26cac]\r\n\r\nCHARTS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  user signed up over time\r\n  value\r\n    value              |▇▃▅█▂▁▃▇▆▃▃▂|  150 → 163\r\n                        2026-08-01 … 2026-08-12\r\n\r\n  user signed up over time\r\n  value\r\n    value              |▅█████▁|  459 → 1,110\r\n                        2026-06-29 … 2026-08-10\r\n\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - All available signup and session data for the period in question ends on 2026-08-12; no tool call returned any rows for the rest of August or for September. This is very likely a data pipeline or connector gap rather than an actual absence of activity, and it makes any month-over-month comparison for August or September unreliable.\r\n  - No GitHub commits were found for acme/product across the"]
[0.000, "o", " whole window checked (July 1 through late August), which is itself surprising for an active product repo and suggests the GitHub connector may not be returning full history either.\r\n  - 2 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- findings[0].claims[0]: Signup and GA4 data indeed cut off at 2026-08-12, but the pageview and trial_started queries returned zero rows for their entire range starting well before that date, so they don't\r\n- findings[0].claims[3]: The Slack message confirms the date and that a team member flagged signups looking down, but nothing in the evidence supports the causal interpretation that this reflects partial-m\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Posthog 'user signed up' and '$pageview' events and GA4 sessions all have no observations after 2026-08-12, despite the question asking about a comparison that requir"]
[0.000, "o", "es August and September data.\r\n  - The 'trial_started' event returned zero rows for the entire 2026-07-01 to 2026-09-21 window, suggesting this event may not be tracked in this project or its data has not synced.\r\n  - 6 of the 10 cited observation(s) returned no results (ga4.get_sessions, github.commits, posthog.event_trend). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exist.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  e58f6ec6  ga4.compare_periods  eval://ga4__compare_periods\r\n  d624355c  ga4.get_sessions  eval://ga4__get_sessions\r\n  72344e52  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  72e7b557  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  09c9c9e8  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  031f54a8  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r\n  ae570c02  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r\n  a79c6f00  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r\n  f3a69518  posthog.event_trend  eval://p"]
